    "title": "BIP352: align reference address decoding with silent payment rules",
    "user": {
      "login": "ginavalent",
      "id": 262554748,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOD6ZEfA",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262554748?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/ginavalent",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/ginavalent",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ginavalent/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ginavalent/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ginavalent/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ginavalent/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ginavalent/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ginavalent/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ginavalent/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ginavalent/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ginavalent/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "BIP 352 specifies that silent payment addresses use Bech32m encoding and defines forward-compatible address decoding rules for versions 0 through 30.\r\n\r\nThe BIP352 reference implementation currently uses the generic SegWit decoder without checking the encoding type, which allows a Bech32 checksum for a silent payment address. It also rejects versions above 16 and passes the complete payload to the spend key parser instead of discarding extension data for future versions.\r\n\r\nUpdate the BIP352-specific decoder to:\r\n\r\n- require Bech32m encoding;\r\n- accept versions 0 through 30 and reject version 31;\r\n- require exactly 66 decoded bytes for version 0;\r\n- accept at least 66 decoded bytes for versions 1 through 30 and consume only the first 66 bytes.\r\n\r\n",
